That is, Laurence Brothers, the author.  (That particular group of
machines at Rutgers are named paul, ringo, etc.)  And this is exactly
the "some reason": some people, like myself (I'm the colleague Rick
mentions) assume that the author's machine will have the lastest
version...

|>I *just* checked ftp.uu.net, which is one of the official archive sites for
|>comp.sources.games, and though the files haven't changed in over 3 years,
|>there is no such bug. In fact, the correct code in the archive is identical to
|>the "fixed" version provided above. This version of Omega (0.75, called Omega3
|>in the archives) was never released with this bug.

The buggy version found on paul is also 0.75.  So comparing version
numbers will not tell you if the bug is present or not.

|Perhaps if comp.sources.games sources were provided in tar format, I
|would be more inclined to use them. As it is, messing with things in
|shar format is a major pain.

"Major pain"?  How are you doing it?  If you refer to having to run
each through sh individually, try this:

stygian% more shem
#/bin/csh -f
foreach file (*)
  echo $file
  sh $file
end

Okay, I concede that having to trim the headers off is suboptimal.
But probably some sed script can be arranged to do that.

